course: dictionary
lesson: 4527
title: Headstone: a grave stone or a building stone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning is meant. Headstone is one of these words. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a grave, or about a building?
explain: A headstone is a stone set at the head of a grave, with the name of the person who died and often a short message. «Ellie brings flowers a few weeks later, and Oliver reads Rest in Peace on a headstone from 1850.» The flowers and the grave show that headstone means the grave stone here.
explain: The second meaning is about buildings: the main stone that holds a building together, also called the keystone or cornerstone. Try your meaning in the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense when you swap in "the stone at a grave", it is the grave meaning; if it only makes sense with "the main stone of a building", that is the right meaning.
fact: A headstone is a stone set at the head of a grave.
fact: A headstone often shows the name of the person who died and a short message.
fact: «Headstone» can also mean the main stone of a building, also called the keystone or cornerstone.
fact: «Burial» means the coffin is put into a grave in the ground and covered with earth; a headstone with the name is added later.
fact: Old headstones, like one from 1850, help people learn about people of the past.
exercise: «Ellie brings flowers a few weeks later, and Oliver reads Rest in Peace on a headstone from 1850.» What is a headstone in this sentence? | A wooden fence around a field | *A stone set at the head of a grave, with a name and often a short message | A small coin used long ago | A bunch of flowers left at the church door
exercise: «Burial» means the coffin is put into a grave and covered with earth. When is the headstone with the name added? | *Later, after the burial | Never, because graves do not have them | Before the burial, to mark the spot | At the end of the school day
exercise: A builder says the headstone is the stone at the top of the arch that holds the whole wall together. What does headstone mean here? | A grave marker with flowers | *The main stone of a building, also called the keystone | A slab of wood on a fence | A stone for skipping on a pond
test: In the phrase «a marble headstone», what is the headstone made of? | Wood | Glass | *Marble | Paper
test: In history lessons, what do pupils learn from reading old headstones? | Songs from long ago | *About people of the past | Ways to build a wall | How to plant flowers
exam: Which sentence uses headstone to mean the main stone of a building? | Families choose a headstone for someone who has died | Ellie lay flowers by the headstone | Oliver read the name carved on the headstone | *The workers set the headstone at the top of the arch, where it holds the whole wall together
